<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Idumaeans</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Idumeans</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Idumaeans were the people of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/idumaea">Idumaea</a>, the region of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/judaea">Judaea</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/negev">Negev</a> settled by Edomites from the 6th century BCE. The Hasmonean ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-hyrcanus">John Hyrcanus</a> conquered them in the late 2nd century BCE and made them adopt <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/judaism">Judaism</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herod-the-great">Herod the Great</a> came from an Idumaean family. In 68 CE Idumaean fighters entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zealots">Zealots</a>' invitation and killed the former high priest Ananus.</p></div>
